	(text "PROPOSED ANALOG FRONT-END  -  one differential channel shown; replicate per ADC input pair (CH0=CT, CH1=PT).\n\nCT (QNCT16L 2000:1):   Rb = 56R   AND populate D1 = 5V bidirectional TVS (e.g. SMAJ5.0CA) across the secondary.\nPT (QNPT03 2mA:2mA):   Rb = 390R,  D1 NOT required (current-type PT is self-limiting). Primary series R lives on the mains-side board.\n\nRb (burden): 0.1% 25ppm - it sets the gain.   Rsp/Rsn = 100R (anti-alias + fault current limit).\nCd = 10nF C0G differential; Ccp/Ccn = 1nF common-mode (anti-alias). Rbp/Rbn = 10k bias to VCM.\nVCM = AVDD/2 from Rvt/Rvb divider + Cv (1uF).  Dp/Dn = BAV199, clamp each ADC pin to AFE_AVDD / AFE_AGND.\n\nNOT CONNECTED - wire it in yourself:  SEC_P/SEC_N -> transformer secondary connector;  AIN_P/AIN_N -> an ADS131M02 AINxP/AINxN pair;\nAFE_AVDD -> your 3V3 (AVDD) rail;  AFE_AGND -> GND.  Delete this note once wired."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38 55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1b2c3d4-0001-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
